    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-uttara-kanda-0021",
      "sequence": 1004,
      "meaning": "In Rama's reign no one is touched by bodily, providential or material affliction. Everyone loves one another and, devoted to the teaching of scripture, follows one's own dharma. Dharma stands complete on all four feet and sin is absent even in dreams. Men and women absorbed in devotion to Rama are entitled to the highest end. There is no untimely death or pain; all bodies are beautiful and free of disease. No one is poor, sorrowful, helpless, foolish or without good qualities. All are unpretentious, devoted to dharma, pure, discerning, virtuous, learned, wise and grateful; cleverness carries no deceit.",
