    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-uttara-kanda-0022",
      "sequence": 1005,
      "meaning": "The earth, girdled by seven seas, has one sovereign—Raghupati of Kosala. Yet countless universes dwell in every hair of the Lord, so such earthly sovereignty is little to him. Even reflecting on his true majesty reveals the inadequacy of describing it. Those who know that greatness nevertheless delight in this human story. Great self-controlled sages call such delight the fruit of knowing him. Neither Shesha nor Sarasvati can describe the happiness and prosperity of Rama's reign. Everyone is generous and helpful, and men and women serve the Brahmins' feet. Every man is devoted to one wife, while wives are faithful to their husbands in thought, word and deed.",
