    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-uttara-kanda-0023",
      "sequence": 1006,
      "meaning": "Trees in forest and grove always flower and bear fruit; elephants and lions live together, while birds and animals forget natural enmity and deepen mutual affection. Flocks call sweetly and roam the forest without fear. A cool fragrant breeze moves gently, carrying nectar as bees hum. Vines and trees yield honey when asked, and cows stream whatever milk is desired. The earth remains rich with crops; in Treta-yuga it displays the ways of Satya-yuga. Mountains reveal mines of many jewels, knowing Rama as the soul of the world and king. Rivers carry excellent, cool, clear and pleasant water. The sea remains within its bounds yet casts jewels upon the shore for people to find. Every pond is crowded with lotuses, and all ten directions are serene.",
