    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-uttara-kanda-0025",
      "sequence": 1008,
      "meaning": "All Rama's brothers serve him devotedly, their love for his feet ever increasing. They watch his lotus face, hoping the compassionate Lord will give them some command. Rama loves his brothers and teaches them ethics and statecraft in many ways. Ayodhya's people remain joyful and enjoy pleasures rare even to gods, yet day and night they pray to the Creator only for love of Raghubira's feet. Sita bears two beautiful sons, Lava and Kusha, whom the Vedas and Puranas celebrate. Both are victorious, humble, abodes of virtue and exquisitely beautiful like reflections of Hari. Each of Rama's brothers likewise has two sons, abundant in beauty, virtue and character.",
