    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-uttara-kanda-0026",
      "sequence": 1009,
      "meaning": "At dawn Rama bathes in the Sarayu and sits in assembly with Brahmins and good people. Vasishtha expounds the Vedas and Puranas; although Rama knows everything, he listens. He eats with his younger brothers, filling all the mothers with joy. Bharata and Shatrughna go with Hanuman to a garden, sit together and ask him to plunge into the deep account of Rama's virtues. Hearing those stainless qualities brings great happiness, and with repeated requests they have Hanuman tell them again. In every home Puranic recitations present Rama's sacred deeds in many forms. Men and women sing his virtues day and night, unaware of time passing.",
