    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-uttara-kanda-0027",
      "sequence": 1010,
      "meaning": "Narada, the Sanaka sages and other lords among seers come every day to behold the Lord of Kosala. On seeing Ayodhya they forget even detachment. Its upper storeys are fashioned from gold and jewels and laid with lovely multicoloured crystal. A beautiful fort surrounds the city on all sides, crowned with battlements in excellent colours. Its many ranks seem like the nine planetary hosts forming armies around Amaravati. Multicoloured crystal paving makes even great sages' minds dance. White mansions rise to touch the sky, their finials seeming to shame the radiance of sun and moon. Gem-built windows shine, and jewelled lamps adorn every home.",
