    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-uttara-kanda-0028",
      "sequence": 1011,
      "meaning": "Everyone plants flower gardens, carefully arranging them in many ways. Graceful vines of many lovely kinds bloom perpetually as though it were spring. Bees hum melodiously while the threefold breeze remains gentle and beautiful. Children lovingly raise many birds, which speak sweetly and fly beautifully. Peacocks, swans, cranes and pigeons add splendour to the houses; seeing their reflections here and there, they call and dance in many ways. Children teach parrots and mynas to say, 'Speak of Rama, Raghupati, protector of the people.' The royal gateway is beautiful in every way, as are the streets, crossroads and markets.",
