    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-uttara-kanda-0029",
      "sequence": 1012,
      "meaning": "A spacious and beautiful ghat stands apart for horses and herds of elephants to drink. There are many delightful water-drawing ghats where men do not bathe. The royal public ghat is excellent in every way, and people of all four varnas bathe there. Temples of the gods line both banks, with lovely gardens on every side. Here and there detached sages and renunciants absorbed in knowledge live beside the river, and groups of sages have planted many beautiful clusters of tulasi along the banks. The city's beauty cannot be described; beyond it the countryside is exquisitely lovely. At the sight of Ayodhya every sin flees amid forests, gardens, wells and ponds.",
