    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-uttara-kanda-0030",
      "sequence": 1013,
      "meaning": "Wherever people gather they sing Raghupati's virtues and teach one another to worship Rama: protector of the surrendered and abode of beauty, character, form and virtue; dark-bodied and lotus-eyed, protecting servants as eyelids protect eyes; bearer of lovely arrows, bow and quiver; battle-firm sun to the lotus-forest of saints; Garuda to the dreadful serpent Time; the desireless one before whom possessiveness bows; hunter of the deer-herds of greed and delusion; lion to the elephant Kama and giver of joy to Hari's people; sun to the dense darkness of doubt and grief; fire that burns the demon forest; Raghubira with Janaka's daughter, destroyer of worldly fear; a mass of snow to the mosquitoes of countless cravings; ever of one essence, unborn and imperishable; delight of sages, remover of Earth's burden and generous Lord of Tulsidas.",
